    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "AS\nAIR SOUTH\nMETRO III\nPASSENGER SAFETY INFORMATION\n\"NO SMOKING\" AND \"FASTEN SEAT BELT\" SIGNS\nFor your safety and comfort. please comply with the \"NO SMOKING\" and\n\"FASTEN SEAT BELT\" signs when they are illuminated. Seat belts should\nbe fastened securely. As a precaution against unexpected turbulence you\nshould keep your seat belt fastened at all times while seated\nTO FASTEN:\nInsert metal tab into\nmetal buckle until it\nsnaps.\nU\nNO SMOKING ALLOWED WHEN OXYGEN IN USE\nTO ADJUST:\nPull end of belt until desired\nsecureness is obtained\nTO REMOVE:\nInsert fingers under buckle\nflange and lift upward\nTire altitudes at which the aircraft operates may\nrequire the use of OXYGEN in the event there is\n• loss of cabin pressure. Should this occur, •\ncrew member will notify you.\ni. Take the mask which is stowed either\nIn back of seat or under sent and promply\nInsert hose plug into OXYGEN outlet recept\nade localed on the center isle above your saal.\n2. Place mask over your nose and mouth.\nBreathe normally.\n3. Acuet headband to hold mask enugly.\n4. Wear mask until advised by crew to remove Il.\n5. If seated in center seat, plug into OXYGEN outler\nreceptade localed above your right shoulder.\nPLEASE DO NOT REMOVE THIS CARD FROM AIRCRAFT-SEE OTHER SIDE",
      "UNLOCKED\nLOCKED\nCLOSE DOOR\nTURN TO LOCK\nLIFE PRESERVER\nLife preservers, if needed, are located under each seat.\nTO PREPARE FOR A LANDING ON WATER:\n1. Follow Instructions of crew.\n2. Pull on Life Preserver (see instructions with Life\nPreserver).\n3. Assume bracing position (see diagram).\n4. After plane stops completely, unfasten seat belt.\n5. After leaving plane, inflate life preserver.\nEMERGENCY EXIT OPERATION\nPASSENGER DOOR OPERATION\n1. Rotate handle in direction of arrow.\n2. Push door OUT.\nNORMAL\nEXIT\nARE\nEXTINGUISHER\nOPEN\nCLOSED\nPULL\nWINDOW EMERGENCY EXIT\n1. Grab HATCH HANDLE. Pull handle and entire\nhatch INWARD AND UP. clear of opening\nEMERGENCY\nEXIT\nFIRE\nEXTINGUISHER\nFIRST AID KIT\nEMERGENCY\nEXIT\n2. Rotate hatch 90° and extend bottom through\nopening. Throw hatch outside aircraft.\nCAUTION\nDO NOT HANDLE OR ATTEMPT TO OPEN THE PASSENGER DOOR\nOR WINDOW EMERGENCY EXITS UNLESS THEY ARE TO BE USED\nIN AN EMERGENCY.\nPLEASE DO NOT REMOVE THIS CARD FROM AIRCRAFT-SEE OTHER SIDE\n2002.\n04"
    ],
